---
source: crates/aether/tests/steps/cli/help.rs
expression: world.cli.stdout()
---
Usage: aether node serve [FLAGS]

Flags:
      --policy <POLICY>                   Old policy file to import on the first start. Later
                                          changes use SQLite.
                                          (default: ~/.aether/policy.json)
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>
                                          (default: ~/.aether/host)
      --port <PORT>
                                          (default: 0)
      --admin-port <ADMIN_PORT>
                                          (default: 0)
      --pact-listen <PACT_LISTEN>         The address the PACT gateway listens on, such as
                                          127.0.0.1:8080. It needs a `pact` section in the policy
                                          and `--admin-port`, which serves the consent page.
      --managed-control <MANAGED_CONTROL>
      --managed-control-certificate <MANAGED_CONTROL_CERTIFICATE>
      --adapter <ADAPTER>                 The agent adapter of this data directory: codex or
                                          connected. The node saves it; later starts keep it.
      --codex-bin <CODEX_BIN>             The Codex binary of the Codex adapter.
                                          [env: AETHER_CODEX_BIN]
                                          (default: codex)
      --relay-url <RELAY_URL>             An iroh relay to reach the node through.
                                          [env: AETHER_RELAY_URL]
      --hub-url <HUB_URL>                 The Aether hub that lets people invite and connect by
                                          name. Defaults to the one set on the page, else the public
                                          hub; `off` turns it off.
                                          [env: AETHER_HUB_URL]
      --directory <DIRECTORY>
      --directory-certificate <DIRECTORY_CERTIFICATE>
      --agent-id <AGENT_ID>               The agent ID in the published directory record. It does
                                          not name invites.
      --address <ADDRESS>
      --scope <SCOPE>
      --capability <CAPABILITY>
      --directory-record-ttl <DIRECTORY_RECORD_TTL>
      --invite-name <INVITE_NAME>         The agent name in invites while this node has no name on
                                          the hub. Defaults to agent- and the first 8 characters of
                                          the endpoint ID.
  -h, --help                              Print help
